7,AIATSIS AustLang Online,https://aiatsis.gov.au/austlang/language/G20,"Mayi is the word for 'speech' or 'language' in two mutually unintelligible but closely related languages from the Gulf area of Queensland, one being Mayi-Kutuna G24 and the other being a dialect chain comprising Mayi-Yapi, Mayi-Thakurti G16, Ngawun G17, Mayi-Kulan G25 and Wunumara G16.1""> G16.1. Breen also says that Mayi is used by speakers to refer to these two languages as a group (1981:2, 15).",Mayi-Yapi,Australian
